# CASE ALIASES -- the former name of a RENAMED tutorial, and its current one
# (declared 2026-10-12, DEV.md 4c C68).
#
# WHAT THIS IS.  A tutorial renamed in the tree keeps a link somebody has
# already shared working: `?case=<old>` in the GUI, `runCase tutorials/<old>`
# on the command line.  This file is the ONE home of that mapping; the GUI
# imports it raw (gui/src/cases/tutorials.ts, `canonicalCaseName`),
# `bin/runCase` reads it, and `bin/curate/check_doc_references.py` lets the
# dated records in DEV.md go on naming a case by the name it had when the
# record was written.
#
# AN ALIAS IS NEVER A SECOND CASE.  It has no directory, it is not listed by
# `listCases`, the case index or the catalogue, and nothing is ever run under
# it -- it resolves, once and announced, to the canonical case.  An old name
# that is a directory again, or a new name that is not one, is a broken alias
# (gui/tests/caseAliases.test.ts refuses both).
#
# FORMAT.  One alias per line, two words separated by spaces:
#
#     <old identifier>   <current identifier>
#
# where an identifier is the case's path RELATIVE TO tutorials/ -- exactly
# the identifier the GUI uses (`plant/<name>`, `steady/<subclass>/<name>`).
# A drilled sub-node of an aliased case resolves through its root
# (`plant/<old>/Converter` -> `plant/<new>/Converter`).  `#` starts a comment.
#
